# Clean Architecture & TDD Guardrails

1. **Separation of Concerns:**
   - Business domain logic must never directly couple with HTTP request/response handlers or raw database drivers.
   - Use Repository or Service patterns to encapsulate persistence.

2. **Test-First Verification:**
   - Any refactoring must be preceded by an audit of existing tests.
   - New endpoints or business functions require corresponding test cases covering edge cases (null inputs, empty arrays, rate-limit triggers).
   - Ensure tests are deterministic and do not depend on active internet connectivity unless explicitly mocked.
